00:32:16.640 --> 00:32:18.940
I just like Jin Ho.

00:32:19.470 --> 00:32:22.940
I'm not trying to join your family or play mom.

00:32:24.300 --> 00:32:26.440
So I thought none of it mattered.

00:32:29.900 --> 00:32:30.939
So?

00:32:30.940 --> 00:32:32.540
But it doesn't matter to your family...

00:32:34.670 --> 00:32:36.740
what kind of person I am...

00:32:39.870 --> 00:32:42.970
or how Jin Ho and I feel about each other.

00:32:49.100 --> 00:32:50.870
I realise now how selfish I have been.

00:32:55.700 --> 00:32:57.000
I'm sorry.

00:32:59.440 --> 00:33:01.000
That's what I came to say.

00:33:47.900 --> 00:33:50.940
("Mrs Dalloway")

00:34:14.570 --> 00:34:15.570
Honey.

00:34:15.970 --> 00:34:16.970
Yes?

00:34:17.700 --> 00:34:18.700
I'm sorry.

00:34:20.170 --> 00:34:21.170
For what?

00:34:24.200 --> 00:34:25.200
For everything.

00:34:26.570 --> 00:34:28.270
You're getting better.

00:34:28.870 --> 00:34:30.400
Everything's going to be okay.

00:34:32.640 --> 00:34:36.040
But don't I smell something burning?

00:34:37.370 --> 00:34:39.940
Oh, no. The sauce. Oh, dear.

00:34:43.040 --> 00:34:46.140
I have to start over. Oh, no. I can't believe this.

00:35:02.570 --> 00:35:04.770
("Mrs Dalloway")

00:35:16.370 --> 00:35:19.810
I wasn't sure if I should celebrate our 35th anniversary...

00:35:20.570 --> 00:35:22.100
or feel sorry for it.

00:35:22.840 --> 00:35:24.440
I just didn't know what to do.

00:35:25.940 --> 00:35:26.940
Instead,

00:35:28.240 --> 00:35:29.640
I've decided to be grateful.

00:35:32.970 --> 00:35:34.340
For 37 years,

00:35:34.870 --> 00:35:36.670
you've always been the same.

00:35:37.640 --> 00:35:40.900
The kind smile you give me.

00:35:42.470 --> 00:35:45.640
The smell of your bland cooking.

00:35:47.100 --> 00:35:50.370
The clumsy sounds you make when you move around.

00:35:52.570 --> 00:35:57.500
The way you talk and laugh at your own unfunny jokes.

00:35:59.840 --> 00:36:00.900
I...

00:36:02.370 --> 00:36:03.670
I love all of you.

00:36:06.170 --> 00:36:07.170
Honey.

00:36:08.240 --> 00:36:09.400
Today is...

00:36:09.900 --> 00:36:11.740
our 35th wedding anniversary.

00:36:14.500 --> 00:36:16.600
Dad, do you need any help?

00:36:16.810 --> 00:36:18.440
What? Perfect timing.

00:36:18.500 --> 00:36:19.500
Wash these for me.

00:36:20.310 --> 00:36:21.440
I'll help too.

00:36:21.540 --> 00:36:23.370
It's okay, Jun Kyung. Go sit down.

00:36:23.600 --> 00:36:27.170
("Mrs Dalloway")

00:37:07.940 --> 00:37:12.040
I should have known how you'd feel about someone like me.

00:37:14.100 --> 00:37:15.200
I was thoughtless.

00:37:18.670 --> 00:37:20.770
At the very least, you just needed some time.

00:37:22.900 --> 00:37:24.000
But not my time.

00:37:27.810 --> 00:37:29.740
But time for yourself and your family.

00:37:39.000 --> 00:37:41.140
I was the most selfish one.

00:37:44.540 --> 00:37:45.940
I convinced myself only I was struggling.

00:37:48.770 --> 00:37:51.000
I cried out that I was the only one who was hurt.

00:37:51.770 --> 00:37:52.970
Aren't you embarrassed?

00:37:56.310 --> 00:37:57.500
I was her.

00:38:00.700 --> 00:38:02.440
And I was Daniel too.

00:38:05.470 --> 00:38:08.040
So who was I to resent anyone or call him a coward?

00:38:13.140 --> 00:38:14.140
Seo Jun Kyung.

00:38:16.740 --> 00:38:19.310
You're so pathetic.

00:39:05.140 --> 00:39:06.240
You're here.

00:39:07.810 --> 00:39:08.900
You got caught in the rain?

00:39:09.740 --> 00:39:11.570
Come on, you should have called if you didn't have an umbrella.

00:39:12.270 --> 00:39:13.940
I just wanted to get rained on.

00:39:14.170 --> 00:39:15.310
But why?

00:39:46.170 --> 00:39:47.170
Yoon Sol.

00:39:48.900 --> 00:39:50.000
Yoon Sol!

00:39:54.340 --> 00:39:55.470
I can't break up with you.

00:39:56.440 --> 00:39:57.700
We're done talking.

00:39:58.270 --> 00:40:01.040
- You might be done, but I'm not. - Hey, Seo Jun Seo!

00:40:08.370 --> 00:40:09.470
Let's go talk outside.

00:40:10.100 --> 00:40:12.310
- I have nothing to say, Jun Seo. - Well, I do.

00:40:12.810 --> 00:40:13.940
Just stop!

00:40:15.740 --> 00:40:17.239
Sol said she was done talking to you.

00:40:17.240 --> 00:40:18.470
Who are you to butt in?

00:40:18.870 --> 00:40:22.270
If you broke up, be an adult. Stop being so pathetic.

00:40:22.340 --> 00:40:23.540
Hey, you stop it too.

00:40:26.440 --> 00:40:27.640
What a loser.

00:40:29.670 --> 00:40:31.869
- You piece of trash. - I said, stop it!

00:40:31.870 --> 00:40:33.270
- You loser. - You!

00:40:33.700 --> 00:40:36.040
- You little... - Come at me.

00:40:36.500 --> 00:40:38.870
- I'll kill you. Let go. - Call the cops.

00:40:38.940 --> 00:40:41.199
- Go on, call the cops! - I told you to let go!

00:40:41.200 --> 00:40:42.440
Let go, you jerk.

00:40:42.810 --> 00:40:43.900
Hey, he bit me.

00:40:44.540 --> 00:40:45.640
What are you doing?

00:40:46.170 --> 00:40:47.170
I told you to stop it!

00:40:49.570 --> 00:40:51.939
- Oh, no. What should we do? - I'm okay.

00:40:51.940 --> 00:40:53.600
Oh, no. Shouldn't you go to the hospital?

00:40:54.070 --> 00:40:55.170
You think it's that bad?

00:40:55.500 --> 00:40:57.669
- Darn. What should I do? - That must hurt a lot.

00:40:57.670 --> 00:40:59.040
You!

00:41:09.170 --> 00:41:10.500
What are you doing here?

00:41:14.370 --> 00:41:15.440
What happened to your face?

00:41:18.040 --> 00:41:22.040
Go beg the professor's forgiveness and say you'll take the offer.

00:41:22.970 --> 00:41:26.770
What kind of idiot throws away a chance like that over a breakup?

00:41:28.670 --> 00:41:30.700
You think your life is over now?

00:41:31.840 --> 00:41:35.000
Why would you go over there just to get a beating like this?

00:41:35.310 --> 00:41:36.600
If my face looks like this,

00:41:37.310 --> 00:41:38.770
you should see the other guy.

00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:41.970
I beat him to a pulp. A complete pulp.

00:41:43.540 --> 00:41:44.600
So...

00:41:45.640 --> 00:41:46.840
do you feel better now?

00:41:51.240 --> 00:41:52.240
No.

00:41:53.540 --> 00:41:54.640
I'm miserable.

00:42:01.500 --> 00:42:02.500
Gosh, it hurts.

00:42:05.770 --> 00:42:06.870
So you can feel pain?

00:42:11.340 --> 00:42:12.440
I'm in agony.

00:42:26.740 --> 00:42:27.740
Hey.

00:42:28.640 --> 00:42:29.740
Why are you crying?

00:42:31.970 --> 00:42:34.100
- Why? - Because I'm in agony.

00:42:36.310 --> 00:42:37.400
Why are you in agony?

00:42:41.540 --> 00:42:43.310
Because I like you.

00:42:49.470 --> 00:42:51.810
The fact that I like someone like you,

00:42:54.170 --> 00:42:56.500
a stupid, pathetic idiot, is absolute torture.

00:43:04.500 --> 00:43:05.500
What?

00:43:14.810 --> 00:43:15.810
I'm saying...

00:43:17.810 --> 00:43:19.270
I like you.

00:44:28.500 --> 00:44:29.970
Jun Kyung, you have a fever.

00:44:30.970 --> 00:44:34.370
I made some porridge. Be sure to eat and take medicine.

00:44:54.070 --> 00:44:55.270
Why aren't you eating?

00:45:03.700 --> 00:45:04.800
It's getting cold.

00:45:10.770 --> 00:45:11.770
Mom.

00:45:15.200 --> 00:45:17.000
I'm just the worst.

00:45:22.340 --> 00:45:23.340
I'm pathetic,

00:45:26.100 --> 00:45:28.340
cowardly, and just plain mean.

00:45:32.800 --> 00:45:36.370
I think Soo Jin was right. I'm just a cold-hearted person.

00:45:41.240 --> 00:45:43.670
The day we first brought Jun Seo home,

00:45:45.140 --> 00:45:48.700
you were so fascinated by him. So you just kept staring.

00:45:51.440 --> 00:45:53.240
You don't remember, do you?

00:45:56.600 --> 00:45:59.870
So when I asked you why, you said...

00:46:00.940 --> 00:46:02.470
Because he's so cute.

00:46:03.340 --> 00:46:06.200
So I said, "Go on. Pat him gently..."

00:46:06.470 --> 00:46:09.570
"and tell him he looks beautiful."

00:46:10.970 --> 00:46:13.670
Do you know what you did then?

00:46:25.640 --> 00:46:28.569
You said your hands were too cold.

00:46:28.570 --> 00:46:29.899
You were worried...

00:46:29.900 --> 00:46:32.040
you might give him a cold if you touched him.

00:46:38.870 --> 00:46:39.870
Jun Kyung.

00:46:41.800 --> 00:46:43.170
You have such a warm heart.

00:46:48.270 --> 00:46:50.200
- Really? - Of course.

00:49:21.470 --> 00:49:22.570
I'm home.

00:49:23.200 --> 00:49:24.600
Did you sleep over at a friend's?

00:49:25.100 --> 00:49:26.840
Hey, you could've at least sent a text.

00:49:28.170 --> 00:49:29.170
Hey.

00:49:30.100 --> 00:49:31.100
What happened to your face?

00:49:32.100 --> 00:49:33.100
I fell.

00:49:33.900 --> 00:49:34.940
Have you been drinking?

00:49:35.370 --> 00:49:36.370
No.

00:49:37.800 --> 00:49:40.300
I was running down the subway stairs.

00:49:41.100 --> 00:49:42.840
You should be more careful. What's all this?

00:49:43.740 --> 00:49:45.499
It's fine. I put some ointment on it.

00:49:45.500 --> 00:49:46.540
It's nothing, really.

00:49:47.140 --> 00:49:49.000
- Seriously. - Gosh.

00:49:49.070 --> 00:49:50.540
That must hurt.

00:49:52.240 --> 00:49:53.840
Why did you suddenly wash Mom's clothes?

00:49:58.300 --> 00:49:59.400
It's nice and sunny.

00:50:16.300 --> 00:50:17.300
Jun Seo.

00:50:19.170 --> 00:50:20.340
Do you want to go see your mom?

00:51:41.900 --> 00:51:42.900
Dad.

00:51:42.901 --> 00:51:44.000
- Yes? - Here's your food.

00:51:50.770 --> 00:51:51.870
Thank you.

00:52:08.370 --> 00:52:11.100
I think I was a little too harsh the other day.

00:52:17.540 --> 00:52:18.540
Not at all.

00:52:21.370 --> 00:52:22.600
From your perspective,

00:52:23.570 --> 00:52:24.900
you had every right to feel that way.

00:52:31.700 --> 00:52:33.340
Anyway, I'm the one...

00:52:39.140 --> 00:52:40.240
who should be sorry.

00:52:55.300 --> 00:52:56.540
Does Jun Seo know?

00:53:02.400 --> 00:53:04.140
If Jun Seo found out, he'd flip out, right?

00:53:05.570 --> 00:53:06.800
Knowing him, yes. Probably.

00:53:08.270 --> 00:53:10.369
You should find the right time to tell him...

00:53:10.370 --> 00:53:12.140
and break the news gently.

00:53:13.900 --> 00:53:15.000
The right time?

00:53:21.640 --> 00:53:24.040
He must be on cloud nine right now.

00:53:25.170 --> 00:53:26.700
Jun Seo? Did something good happen?

00:53:36.300 --> 00:53:37.300
I'm saying...

00:53:39.200 --> 00:53:40.700
I like you.

00:53:57.270 --> 00:53:59.040
I heard you got the research internship.

00:54:00.940 --> 00:54:01.940
Yes.

00:54:03.700 --> 00:54:04.870
I was bragging about you.

00:54:05.300 --> 00:54:07.270
That you beat out all the master's and PhD candidates for the spot.

00:54:08.870 --> 00:54:10.140
Congratulations. Seriously.

00:54:11.600 --> 00:54:14.400
Hey, eat up, all right? Have some of these perilla leaves.

00:54:26.100 --> 00:54:27.140
Actually,

00:54:28.140 --> 00:54:29.240
I quit.

00:54:31.840 --> 00:54:32.940
- Why? - Why?

00:54:35.640 --> 00:54:38.300
It just sort of happened.

00:54:39.770 --> 00:54:42.540
- Wait, why? - What? Why would you pass up...

00:54:44.140 --> 00:54:46.270
a great opportunity like that? Why...

00:54:48.040 --> 00:54:49.600
Sol and I broke up.

00:54:51.570 --> 00:54:52.570
What?

00:54:59.640 --> 00:55:01.100
I'm sorry, Dad.

00:55:01.840 --> 00:55:03.270
I know how happy you were.

00:55:04.240 --> 00:55:07.200
- No, I wasn't that... - What a dumb reason to...

00:55:20.770 --> 00:55:22.570
You must have been really upset, Jun Seo.

00:55:27.200 --> 00:55:30.740
Why'd you stop? Go on, lay into me like you normally would.

00:55:32.270 --> 00:55:34.400
I totally deserve it.

00:55:36.170 --> 00:55:37.170
Forget it.

00:55:38.270 --> 00:55:41.600
The fact is, you earned that internship on your own merit.

00:55:45.540 --> 00:55:46.540
That's a relief.

00:55:47.070 --> 00:55:50.100
I was so worried about how I was going to tell you all.

00:56:01.570 --> 00:56:02.640
I miss Bom.

00:56:03.270 --> 00:56:04.940
Dad, isn't your friend going on a trip again soon?

00:56:05.540 --> 00:56:06.800
You should bring Bom over again.

00:56:08.700 --> 00:56:09.700
Who's Bom?

00:56:10.170 --> 00:56:11.400
Dad's friend's dog.

00:56:14.470 --> 00:56:17.440
Bom's owner isn't just my friend.

00:56:19.070 --> 00:56:20.070
What?

00:56:23.670 --> 00:56:25.440
She's my girlfriend's dog.

00:56:29.200 --> 00:56:30.200
What?

00:56:41.970 --> 00:56:43.700
We've been seeing each other for about two months.

00:56:45.300 --> 00:56:48.500
And we've known each other for about three.

00:56:50.900 --> 00:56:51.900
It's just...

00:56:52.970 --> 00:56:55.999
Neither of us really made a move. We just fell for each other hard.

00:56:56.000 --> 00:56:57.000
Dad.

00:56:57.500 --> 00:57:00.170
I don't think we need all the details.

00:57:03.970 --> 00:57:06.640
Wait a minute. Your timing is pretty similar.

00:57:07.700 --> 00:57:09.300
So are things still going well with the guy next door?

00:57:09.700 --> 00:57:12.000
That's right. How are things with your guy?

00:57:12.600 --> 00:57:13.600
Well...

00:57:18.470 --> 00:57:19.470
What?

00:57:21.140 --> 00:57:22.270
Did you get dumped already?

00:57:22.700 --> 00:57:24.640
The thing is...

00:57:27.600 --> 00:57:30.340
The thing is, he actually...

00:57:33.040 --> 00:57:35.870
has a son. He's in eighth grade.

00:57:36.840 --> 00:57:37.840
- What? - What?

00:57:38.340 --> 00:57:39.740
Hey! Watch out!

00:57:46.500 --> 00:57:49.500
Nobody move. Stay still.

00:57:49.700 --> 00:57:51.140
- What? - Hold on.

00:57:53.870 --> 00:57:56.439
Wait, so he was married?

00:57:56.440 --> 00:57:58.039
Are you crazy? Why would I date a married man?

00:57:58.040 --> 00:58:01.170
So he's not married? Thank goodness. That's a relief.

00:58:01.540 --> 00:58:02.969
He's cute. A really sweet kid.

00:58:02.970 --> 00:58:06.600
He's cute? Gosh, that's a relief too.

00:58:07.600 --> 00:58:10.400
No! We're going to fall. Don't move! Stop!

00:58:10.470 --> 00:58:13.140
- Don't even breathe. - Don't breathe.

00:58:15.300 --> 00:58:16.970
We came to see Mom.

00:58:18.100 --> 00:58:20.870
- And we almost saw her for real. - You little...

00:58:20.940 --> 00:58:23.970
Sorry, I shouldn't have said that. I'm sorry.

00:58:25.940 --> 00:58:26.940
By the way, are you guys...

00:58:27.700 --> 00:58:28.700
okay?

00:58:29.570 --> 00:58:30.900
Yes, I'm fine.

00:58:31.270 --> 00:58:32.740
I think I'm okay too.

00:58:33.540 --> 00:58:35.570
- How about you, Dad? - Yes, I'm fine too.

00:58:36.240 --> 00:58:39.240
As long as everyone's okay, that's a huge relief.

00:58:40.940 --> 00:58:42.000
But look at us.

00:58:42.840 --> 00:58:44.300
Are we actually okay?

00:58:50.300 --> 00:58:52.140
- Hey, Jun Seo. - Yes?

00:58:52.200 --> 00:58:53.870
Try turning the wheel just slightly to the left.

00:58:55.940 --> 00:58:58.270
No, don't! Stop it. Just stay still.

00:58:59.570 --> 00:59:03.770
(Love Me)

00:59:36.040 --> 00:59:38.000
Was it something you did in the heat of the moment?

00:59:39.400 --> 00:59:41.870
I felt like I owed you an apology.

00:59:42.100 --> 00:59:45.370
My feelings are my problem, and I expect nothing from you.

00:59:45.770 --> 00:59:47.440
So you don't have to say anything else.

00:59:48.800 --> 00:59:51.070
I thought we were coming to the campsite for fun.

00:59:51.170 --> 00:59:54.240
But I never imagined that we'd come here to buy it.

00:59:54.540 --> 00:59:57.640
It's a house without its owner. It's filled only with memories.

00:59:57.940 --> 01:00:00.040
I'm thinking of selling this house.

01:00:01.500 --> 01:00:03.300
The kids will understand, right?

01:00:04.240 --> 01:00:07.499
I want to get along with Daniel.

01:00:07.500 --> 01:00:08.670
Why?

01:00:09.040 --> 01:00:10.339
You don't think I can?

01:00:10.340 --> 01:00:11.400
Daniel.

01:00:12.000 --> 01:00:13.240
I don't like her.

01:00:14.140 --> 01:00:16.040
Can't you break up with her?

01:00:16.770 --> 01:00:20.670
Something about this spring feels unusually bitter.

01:00:21.040 --> 01:00:23.000
Don't you think it's going to be an especially cruel one?